Concern: the training tape attaches to a RadCtx, and the Engine is the only owner of it
Upstream: not-submitted

The tape (0101) attaches to a RadCtx through rad_set_issue_observer, but the Engine never hands its
RadCtx out. Without a way in, `r97train ops` and the op-inventory host test would have to stand up
their own prefill loop and would record something other than the step the engine actually runs. The
hook is one accessor on Engine: rank 0's context, between start() and serve().

--- a/core/engine.h
+++ b/core/engine.h
@@ -84,6 +84,13 @@
     const Program& program() const;
     const Config&  config()  const { return cfg_; }
 
+    /* Rank 0's runtime context, for an issue observer (rad_runtime.h): the Engine owns the only
+     * RadCtx, so a tape (patches/training/0101) has no other way in. Null before start(). Attach
+     * between start() and serve() and detach before the Engine dies; a tensor-parallel engine
+     * records rank 0 only: the other ranks issue the same ops on their shards, and one tape is
+     * one stream. */
+    RadCtx* issue_ctx() const;
+
     /* The startup report (core/diag/diag.h): every option with its value and source, the
      * machine, and what on it costs speed or correctness. serve() prints it with RAD_OK before
      * listening; main prints it with the error start() or serve() failed with, so a server that
--- a/core/engine_bringup.cpp
+++ b/core/engine_bringup.cpp
@@ -4277,6 +4277,11 @@
 
 const Program& Engine::program() const { return ranks_[0]->program; }
 
+RadCtx* Engine::issue_ctx() const {
+    if (ranks_.empty() || !ranks_[0]) return nullptr;
+    return &ranks_[0]->ctx;
+}
+
